{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993644504355001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"rot-tarn-revel","assignee":"Joe Oakhart","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"810bd573c77ed258c8f4d21d7361970c0bf4d57d","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 5bfc-c3f8-72d6-40dc","material: c4c052ebd3608e2f","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 13","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","verified-at-sha:810bd573c77ed258c8f4d21d7361970c0bf4d57d","dep absent docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md","dep absent infra/bootstrap/main.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/backup.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/dns.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/iam.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/main.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/network.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/ssm.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/user_data.sh","dep absent infra/terraform/variables.tf","dep absent infra/terraform/versions.tf","dep 8114a74ad5c7447358933690584c4e1ada9cba91343a53f7023aad248447e6d5 pyproject.toml"],"signature":"29064d0c1c7afdd7a5650fa08cb336dd8930aa1836314e0370a920e3b90a95db","signed_at":1782779114383414000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":15},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"DERISK (E1/E2/E3, real AWS CLI as root of acct 896586841071, us-east-1):\n- Default VPC exists: vpc-01fb22d3dd50a364c (172.31.0.0/16).\n- AL2023 arm64 AMI resolvable via SSM public param /aws/service/ami-amazon-linux-latest/al2023-ami-kernel-default-arm64 (currently ami-06c84fbfd615657d3) — use the SSM param, not a hardcoded id.\n- t4g.large offered in all us-east-1 AZs (a/b/c/d/e/f).\n- Route53: PUBLIC hosted zone solutions.navateam.com EXISTS in this account (Z05558453EZPQLHKC20IQ) — create rebar.solutions.navateam.com as an A record (-> EIP) directly in this zone. (Parent is solutions.navateam.com, not navateam.com.)\n- SSM SecureString put -> get --with-decryption -> delete round-trip validated (the secrets-at-boot pattern); no lingering param.\n- run-instances DRY-RUN with the exact shape (t4g.large, ami-06c84fbfd615657d3, gp3 encrypted root, IMDSv2 HttpTokens=required, default subnet) returned 'Request would have succeeded' — call + IAM perms validated without launching.","timestamp":1782686146177655001}],"created_at":1782685470035347001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"# S1 — Terraform base: EC2 box, networking, DNS subdomain, IAM, SSM secrets, state/backups\n\n## Why\nThe PoC needs one cost-conscious, reproducible AWS host for Gerrit + the rebar MCP.\nCodifying it as IaC is runtime-free and delivers the freeze-and-restore RTO (rebuild\nfrom Terraform) without adding cost — so it serves P3 (reusability) without touching\nP2 (cost). Everything else in this epic lands on this substrate.\n\n## What\n- One-time bootstrap (`infra/bootstrap/`): an S3 state bucket (versioning + SSE) created\n  by a small standalone config applied ONCE manually — this breaks the state-backend\n  chicken-and-egg (TF can't store state in a bucket it hasn't created yet). Its bucket\n  name feeds the main config's backend block.\n- `infra/terraform/` using roll-your-own raw resources (the ec2-instance module adds\n  indirection at N=1):\n  - `versions.tf`: `required_version = \">= 1.10\"` (S3 native `use_lockfile` needs TF\n    >=1.10; older TF SILENTLY ignores it and runs with NO locking) + `required_providers`\n    (aws ~> 5).\n  - `t4g.large` (Graviton, ~8 GB) on AL2023 arm64 — AMI resolved via the SSM public param\n    `/aws/service/ami-amazon-linux-latest/al2023-ami-kernel-default-arm64` (NOT a hardcoded\n    id); gp3 root + a separate gp3 data volume mounted at `/var/gerrit` with\n    `lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }`; IMDSv2 required.\n  - Default VPC; security group inbound 443 (HTTPS) + 29418 (Gerrit SSH); admin access via\n    SSM Session Manager (no inbound 22). One Elastic IP, also `prevent_destroy = true`.\n  - Route 53 A record `rebar.solutions.navateam.com` -> EIP in the existing public zone\n    `Z05558453EZPQLHKC20IQ` (solutions.navateam.com).\n  - IAM instance role: attach `AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore` (REQUIRED for Session Manager\n    — the sole admin path) + SSM Parameter Store read (+ KMS decrypt) + CloudWatch basic.\n  - SSM Parameter Store SecureString params (placeholders) for the Gerrit secrets, the\n    GitHub replication deploy key, the rebar MCP HMAC signing key, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.\n  - `user_data.sh` (cloud-init): at first boot, fetch the SSM SecureString params via the\n    instance role and write them to a `chmod 600` `.env` (NO plaintext secrets in user_data\n    itself); IMDSv2 enforced.\n  - Terraform S3 backend with `use_lockfile=true` (no DynamoDB); DLM daily EBS snapshots of\n    the data volume with a bounded `retain_rule { count = 7 }`.\n- Packaging: ensure `infra/` is excluded from ALL distribution channels.\n\n## Scope\nIn: the bootstrap + TF base + DNS subdomain + IAM + SSM scaffolding + boot script +\nstate/backup config + the packaging exclusion. Out: Gerrit/MCP containers (S2), Gerrit\nconfig (S3), replication (S5), GitHub lockdown (S6).\n\n## Files\n- `infra/bootstrap/main.tf` (one-time state bucket: versioning + SSE)\n- `infra/terraform/{versions,main,network,iam,ssm,dns,backup}.tf`\n- `infra/terraform/user_data.sh` (SSM-pull -> chmod 600 .env boot script)\n- `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist]` include is `[\"src/rebar\",\"tests\",\"README.md\"]`\n  so `infra/` is excluded by default — add an explicit exclude + a build-artifact check)\n- `docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md` (ADR capturing the three novel decisions: the S3 state-bucket bootstrap chicken-and-egg pattern, the no-DynamoDB S3-native locking choice gated on Terraform >=1.10, and the `/rebar/prod/*` SSM parameter naming contract — each with rationale)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `terraform -chdir=infra/terraform validate` and `plan` succeed (TF >=1.10 enforced via\n      `required_version`); `apply` stands up a reachable `t4g.large` with EIP, gp3 root + data\n      volume mounted at `/var/gerrit`, IMDSv2 enforced.\n- [ ] The state-bucket bootstrap (`infra/bootstrap/`) is documented as a one-time manual apply;\n      the main config's S3 backend uses `use_lockfile=true` (no DynamoDB), gated by `required_version >= 1.10`.\n- [ ] The stateful data volume AND the EIP carry `lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }` (no silent\n      destroy/recreate of Gerrit data on apply/rename/AMI change).\n- [ ] `rebar.solutions.navateam.com` resolves (Route 53 A -> EIP in zone Z05558453EZPQLHKC20IQ); SG\n      allows 443 + 29418; admin access via SSM Session Manager with the role granting\n      `AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore` and no inbound 22.\n- [ ] `user_data.sh` pulls the SSM SecureString params at boot to a `chmod 600` file; no plaintext\n      secrets appear in user_data.\n- [ ] DLM creates daily snapshots of the data volume with bounded retention (e.g. `retain_rule count=7`).\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md` exists and records the three novel architectural decisions with rationale: (1) the S3 state-bucket bootstrap chicken-and-egg pattern, (2) the no-DynamoDB S3-native `use_lockfile` locking choice gated on Terraform >=1.10, and (3) the `/rebar/prod/*` SSM parameter naming contract.\n- [ ] A built sdist AND wheel contain NO `infra/` files (deterministic check: `python -m build` then\n      grep the artifacts for `infra/`). Homebrew + the MCP registry INHERIT this exclusion because both\n      package the same built artifact (the formula builds from the sdist/release; the registry ships the\n      wheel) — so the sdist/wheel check is the single source of truth, documented as such.\n\n## Round-7 remediation\n- **DLM service role (G6):** AWS Data Lifecycle Manager assumes its OWN IAM role (trust principal `dlm.amazonaws.com`, perms `ec2:CreateSnapshot`/`CreateTags`/`DescribeVolumes`/`DeleteSnapshot`). S1 creates this DLM service role and wires its ARN into the `aws_dlm_lifecycle_policy` `execution_role_arn` — without it DLM silently creates no snapshots.\n- [ ] The DLM lifecycle policy references a created DLM service role (trust `dlm.amazonaws.com`) and is ENABLED (verified it would snapshot the data volume, not silently no-op).\n\n## Plan-review remediation (Round-11, 2026-06-29)\n- SSM SecureString scaffolding extended so no downstream lookup fails: ADD `/rebar/prod/alert-endpoint` (consumed by S7 `monitoring.tf`) and `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token` (consumed by S4a) to the enumerated placeholder params.\n- Ownership contracts: S1 CREATES the single EC2 instance role (S2/S4a only add separately-named scoped inline policies, never re-declare it). S1 OWNS the DLM service role + `aws_dlm_lifecycle_policy` (retain count=7); S7 only asserts/monitors it (no second DLM resource).\n\nAdded ACs:\n- [ ] SSM placeholder set includes `/rebar/prod/alert-endpoint` and `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token` (in addition to Gerrit secrets, deploy key, HMAC key, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)\n- [ ] The EC2 instance role and the DLM lifecycle policy + DLM service role are created HERE and only here; ADR-0012 records the single-owner contract (S2/S4a attach scoped policies; S7 only monitors DLM)\n\n\n## Round-12 plan-review remediation (2026-06-29 — recalibrated gate BLOCK)\nTwo blocking findings fixed; advisories triaged and folded in.\n\n**Blocking (resolved):**\n- **B1 — bootstrap state-bucket destruction guard:** the `aws_s3_bucket` in `infra/bootstrap/main.tf` carries `lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }` (the state bucket is the third stateful resource alongside the data volume + EIP; without it a `terraform destroy` of the bootstrap stack deletes all TF state, defeating the rebuild-from-Terraform RTO). Destroying it requires an explicit state migration first; recorded in ADR-0012.\n- **B2 — idempotent data-volume init:** `user_data.sh` MUST check-before-mkfs — `if ! blkid <device> >/dev/null 2>&1; then mkfs.xfs <device>; fi` — so an instance replacement (e.g. the SSM AMI pointer advancing) re-mounts the existing `/var/gerrit` volume WITHOUT reformatting. `prevent_destroy` guards the Terraform resource; the blkid guard guards the in-guest filesystem (mkfs is a runtime op TF cannot prevent).\n\n**Advisories folded in:**\n- **Enumerated SSM param names** (the `/rebar/prod/*` naming contract, recorded in ADR-0012): `/rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key`, `/rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-hmac-signing-key`, `/rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key`, `/rebar/prod/alert-endpoint`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token`.\n- **Placeholder lifecycle + fail-fast:** params are created with a `CHANGEME` placeholder; the operator MUST populate real values before the S2 apply. `user_data.sh` exits non-zero (cloud-init marks the instance failed) if any fetched value still equals the placeholder sentinel — never silently writes broken config.\n- **IAM least privilege:** the instance-role SSM read + `kms:Decrypt` is scoped to `arn:aws:ssm:<region>:<account>:parameter/rebar/prod/*` (no wildcard), referencing `data.aws_caller_identity`.\n- **AMI drift:** `aws_instance` carries `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [ami] }`; an AMI upgrade is a deliberate runbook step, not a side effect of a routine apply.\n- **Explicit volume sizes:** gp3 root 30 GB, data 50 GB, surfaced as variables.\n- **`infra/terraform/variables.tf`** surfaces `snapshot_retention_count` (default 7), `instance_type` (default `t4g.large`), and the volume sizes.\n\n**Added / updated ACs:**\n- [ ] `infra/bootstrap/main.tf` state bucket has `lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }`.\n- [ ] `user_data.sh` volume init is idempotent (blkid check before mkfs); a re-run on instance replacement does not reformat the data volume.\n- [ ] Instance-role SSM/KMS policy is scoped to `parameter/rebar/prod/*` (no wildcard), verified against the attached policy.\n- [ ] `aws_instance` has `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [ami] }`; AMI upgrade is a documented runbook step.\n- [ ] The SSM placeholder param set is enumerated by exact name and recorded in ADR-0012; `user_data.sh` fails fast on an unpopulated placeholder sentinel.\n- [ ] gp3 volumes have explicit sizes (root 30 GB, data 50 GB) surfaced as Terraform variables in `variables.tf`.\n- [ ] ADR-0012 records FOUR decisions: (1) the S3 state-bucket bootstrap chicken-and-egg, (2) no-DynamoDB S3-native `use_lockfile` gated on TF >=1.10, (3) the `/rebar/prod/*` SSM naming contract, (4) the single-owner contract for the EC2 instance role + DLM policy.\n\n\n## Round-13 plan-review remediation (NVMe device naming on Nitro)\n- **B2 refinement — NVMe-aware device resolution:** on t4g.large (Graviton/Nitro) AL2023 presents EBS volumes as NVMe devices (`/dev/nvme1n1`…), NOT the Xen `device_name` (`/dev/xvdf`) Terraform sets. `user_data.sh` therefore resolves the data volume's real device DYNAMICALLY by its EBS volume id rather than hardcoding a name: the volume id is passed into the script via `templatefile()`, and the script matches it against the NVMe controller serial (`for d in /dev/nvme*n1; do nvme id-ctrl -v \"$d\" 2>/dev/null | grep -q \"$VOL_NODASH\" && DATA_DEV=$d; done`, or equivalently the AL2023 `/dev/disk/by-id/nvme-Amazon_Elastic_Block_Store_vol...` symlink / `ebsnvme-id`). Only after resolving `DATA_DEV` does the blkid-before-mkfs guard run, so the guard targets the correct device on Nitro. Added AC.\n- [ ] `user_data.sh` resolves the data volume's NVMe device path dynamically by EBS volume id (not a hardcoded `/dev/xvdf`); the blkid-before-mkfs guard then runs against the resolved device. Verified the resolved device matches the attached data volume on the live t4g.large.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/bootstrap/main.tf","reason":"one-time S3 state-bucket bootstrap (versioning+SSE+prevent_destroy)"},{"path":"infra/terraform/versions.tf","reason":"TF>=1.10 + provider pins + S3 backend use_lockfile"},{"path":"infra/terraform/main.tf","reason":"EC2 t4g.large, EBS volumes, EIP, ignore_changes ami"},{"path":"infra/terraform/network.tf","reason":"default VPC data + security group 443/29418"},{"path":"infra/terraform/iam.tf","reason":"instance role + SSM/KMS scoped policy + DLM service role"},{"path":"infra/terraform/ssm.tf","reason":"SSM SecureString placeholder params"},{"path":"infra/terraform/dns.tf","reason":"Route53 A record"},{"path":"infra/terraform/backup.tf","reason":"DLM daily snapshot policy"},{"path":"infra/terraform/variables.tf","reason":"tunable vars (retention, instance_type, sizes)"},{"path":"infra/terraform/user_data.sh","reason":"SSM->.env boot, NVMe-aware idempotent volume init"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"exclude infra/ from sdist+wheel"},{"path":"docs/adr/0012-iac-foundations.md","reason":"ADR with four decisions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","d251-05e1-eb55-43b2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d251-05e1-eb55-43b2","parent_status_uuid":"a47878b9-e3a5-441d-a4c1-7b817faa4c63","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["infra","aws","terraform"],"ticket_id":"5bfc-c3f8-72d6-40dc","ticket_type":"story","title":"infra: S1 — Terraform base (EC2, networking, DNS subdomain, IAM, SSM secrets, state/backups)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b355c849-bf93-4da3-a2d1-d48de17922c9","ac21b0b1-a50d-4744-90d1-d80f18e5af37","1e9342d3-27d1-4fb6-925d-2476633a5710","ce698f5b-ed4f-422d-8f88-00ae55f58063","02adfc1f-7a05-4189-99f5-0fc1d291cf42","70b232b1-57bb-4025-b18d-e191dbfbe884","5dd54c52-16e9-4b43-9bbd-9b3e0a00f0df","5627618f-1866-4e35-8e05-bea268fa27c8","5221215e-35d5-4d37-8235-843f7705b434","599b721b-e65c-4bf5-958e-a54a40d46bad","1b102b42-917a-44ad-8fbf-55cb4e6b24f2","8c1b175c-4d93-49e8-bd60-d11910f29b61","3b8fe565-3aac-4e3c-9225-76d06dfbbca5","1bbf294b-0c0a-4a7a-b710-fb5382d889a8","f0e6f77b-fa79-48c0-b2b5-b37e912ad435","1a96465b-3e1f-4188-b5c5-a45b87f81709","e802bf38-b0f5-4efd-9560-7b153a7e1c33","d11d5973-c51b-4f03-94ac-717adba27224","acbaae11-c751-4428-b240-06e8e444a592","6fb70c44-c21a-4eb3-a5a7-b5703b524f79","700b01fd-1e45-4910-8653-b8ae9bce15b7","64601d0e-106f-4c75-89c8-61cb071c6a70","a47878b9-e3a5-441d-a4c1-7b817faa4c63","33b635db-de18-4561-9c2e-5d5a6e31a5c4","1131e53f-a5f5-4ef3-bd2d-a7756d840f0a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993644504355001,"uuid":"1b4e83c3-2a31-4867-a542-c22635066201"}